{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nUmbrella for the 2026-06-09 post-extraction audit, workstream 1: migration artifacts no longer relevant in standalone rebar — remaining dso references, orphaned/unreachable engine scripts, half-implemented features stranded by the extraction, stale docs. Previously-deferred Tier-D items (dso-named reconciler internals, dso_label Jira scheme, plugins.dso.* module keys) are IN SCOPE: rebar is not dso-compatible and prior dso functionality can be freely broken. Every orphan claim was verified by reachability grep before its child ticket was filed. Child tasks carry per-instance evidence and remediation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Zero unreachable files under src/rebar/_engine/ (reachability map re-run clean)\n- [ ] No rebar runtime writes under .claude/ (child story petty-pixel-rat)\n- [ ] Final residue grep documented with a written justification per remaining hit\n- [ ] All child tickets closed (deletions with their locking tests removed in the same commit; full suite green each time).\n- [ ] git grep -iE 'dso|brainstorm|preplanning|scrutiny' over src/ and docs/ returns only deliberate, documented residue (e.g. historical provenance ids if kept).\n- [ ] The published wheel ships no orphaned engine files."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785007098550957001,"uuid":"03370703-cbeb-43d2-8f41-cf352a486a4c"}